Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA  Left lobular carcinoma  positive margins  on DCIS on lump at Brigham and Women s Hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  IN SITU CARCINOMA  SCATTERED FOCI AROUND THE BIOPSY CAVITY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The in situ carcinoma displays both ductal and lobular features  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  LYMPH NODE  INTRAMAMMARY   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Lymph Node  Intramammary   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 6cm fragment of breast tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x 5 8cm skin ellipse with a 3 5cm central  well healed  curvilinear scar and containing two sutures designated by the surgeon as  short superior  long lateral   The specimen is inked black superiorly and blue inferiorly and sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm blood filled biopsy cavity surrounded by a rubbery  ill defined  white fibrotic area which focally extends to the inked margin  superior   Also located in the lateral end of the specimen is a 0 5cm intraparenchymal lymph node  SECTION CODE A  Biopsy cavity with superior margin  B H  Representative sections of biopsy cavity  I J  Representative tissue away from biopsy cavity  J contains intraparenchymal lymph node   Resident  LISA A  GALLAGHER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Richard Graham Pingree  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION   report_end  , No.
