en receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast carcinoma   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked superior half in black  the inferior half in blue  and overinked the anterior with green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm white firm stellate area located 0 3cm of the anterior  closest resection margin  in the lateral half of the specimen  A biopsy cavity is present in the medial half  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in A D and the biopsy cavity in E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents  is a fragment of soft tan adipose tissue measuring 6 x 5 x 1cm with an ellipse of skin measuring 2 x  5cm  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in F through I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional interior margin  right breast  are two fragments of adipose tan soft tissue measuring in aggregate 2 x 2 x  5cm  One fragment contains firm  nodular fibrous area that measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 x  5cm  The specimen is submitted entirely in J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  right breast  is a fragment of tan  fibroadipose tissue measuring 10 x 2 x  5cm  Representative sections are submitted in K through O  Please note that there are additional specimens taken on the yellow sheet called  additional axillary tissue  that was not received  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA GROSSLY NEGATIVE MARGINS  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST   ADDITIONAL AXILLA TISSUE    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EXCIS PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION , No.
