wer inner quadrant of the breast and  does not in the remote biopsy site in the lower outer breast  In addition the  current carcinoma is histomorphologically distinct from the previously diagnosed    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   left breast carcinoma  To evaluate for in situ carcinoma   immunostained slides for calponin and smooth myosin heavy chain  were examined   the findings support the diagnosis     D  BREAST EXCISION  RIGHT DUCTAL MARGIN   Breast parenchyma  there is no evidence of malignancy     E  BREAST MASTECTOMY  RIGHT   Fibrocystic changes  there is no evidence of malignancy     F  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISION  RIGHT AXILLA  541   Two lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  see note      NOTE  Immunostained slides for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  were examined on tissue levels        Electronically Signed Out By Dennis C Sgroi MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       PROCEDURES ADDENDA    HER 2 Quantitation by Immunohistochemistry  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    C  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The invasive tumor cells show focal moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2  protein     Note   HER 2 quantitation  The tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated  visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete  membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete or incomplete  membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in    10  of tumor cells     Reference  ASCO CAP  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Testing Guideline Update  Arch Pathol Lab Med   doi 10  REMOVED_CASE_ID  arpa  REMOVED_CASE_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SA         