Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WITH MUCINOUS DIFFERENTIATION   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SPANNING AN AREA OF REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED FROM THE GLASS SLIDE  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE POSTERIOR  BLUE  INKED MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW AND INTERMEDIATE GRADES WITHIN AND AWAY FROM THE MASS  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED  BLACK  ANTERIOR MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL DEEP   TISSUE  BREAST PARENCHYMA   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  TISSUE  NERVE AND SKELETAL MUSCLE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OUT OF 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  There is a long suture designating the lateral margin and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked in black and the superior lateral and posterior margin are overlayered with green  red and blue ink  respectively  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate tan  white firm mass present at 0 3cm from the anterior margin  The surrounding breast tissue is white and firm and extends to the medial  superior and posterior margins  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  including the closest margin  The rest of the sections are submitted in cassettes B J  I and J are the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left additional deep breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fatty tissue  No mass is identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K and L  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  Multiple lymph nodes are disected from this fatty tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes M Q  B and 