g the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  92  to chromosome 17 signals  84  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Thursday May 14   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 38 08AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Excision PART B  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART C  Breast  Right   Final Lateral Shaved Margin    Excision PART D  Breast  Right   Final Anterior Shaved Margin    Excision PART E  Breast  Right   Final Superior Shaved Margin    Excision PART F  Breast  Righ  report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FOUR MICROSCOPIC FOCI  RANGING IN SIZE FROM REMOVED_DATE TO 0 5CM  WELL DIFFERENTIAL  SEVERAL FOCI LESS THAN 0 1CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The ductal carcinoma in situ extensively involves sclerosing adenosis  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  INVOLVING ALL TEN SLIDES  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACE  SEE NOTE   B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH NODULAR ADENOSIS AND PROMINENT SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 18 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast which is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm area containing an ill defined firm nodule  0 6cm in greatest dimension  The remainder of the specimen is composed of fatty tissue  No frozen done  The entire specimen is submitted in A through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal dense  fibrotic cut surface  which is mixed with areas of adipose tissue and breast parenchyma  No discrete lesion is identified  No frozen section is done  The majority   90   of the specimen is submitted in K through T  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROUS AREAS AND 0 6CM NODULE SUGGESTIVE OF FIBROADENOMA  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR IDENTIFIED  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING TUMOR SEEN  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  Eugene Francis Ruffolo  M D  PART