eptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue with two needle localizations  Taking the area where the needles exit the specimen as the proximal end  the specimen is inked  the needles removed  and the specimen is sectioned proximal to distal to reveal a hard  white to tan 6mm nodule approximately 2mm from the nearest inked margin  which corresponds to a prominent mammographic lesion  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through M  Cassette A represents the most proximal portion  cassette M represents the most distal portion  and cassettes B through G represent the nodule  No frozen done  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   FIRM SUSPICIOUS LESION 6MM IN DIAMETER  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Paul Clarke Shellito  M D  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST LESION   report_end  , No.
