ining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 56     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm  with an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 13 0cm  A nipple on the skin ellipse is grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm  Sectioning reveals a white firm mass located in the lateral part of the specimen at the beginning of the axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm  The lesion approaches the deep resection margin which is the closest margin grossly to 1 0cm  Away from this area is a poorly difined  firm yellow white nodule  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Section Code  A B  deep margins which are the closest margin  C D E  representative sections of the lesion  Two additional areas are submitted in cassettes O and P  respectively  A white  firm lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm is submitted in cassettes Q T  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  Representative sections of lymph node are submitted in cassettes G through N  Note that the largest lymph node which is bisected and submitted in half in cassette I measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
