Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 16 12 CLINICAL DATA  Local recurrence after lumpectomy and radiation in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE OR IN SITU TUMOR  ONE BENIGN LYMPH NODE  FROM LATERAL ASPECT  MINOR FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  WITH RARE MICROCALCIFICATIONS Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 13 57                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm simple mastectomy specimen surfaced by an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm tan skin ellipse  There is an undesignated short suture on one aspect  taken as superior  and an undesignated long suture at one tail end  taken as lateral   There is an eccentric unremarkable nipple areolar complex which abuts the inferior skin margin  Submitted additionally there is a 6 0cm in length linear  well healed scar located 11 5cm superolaterally from the nipple  The scar comes within 0 8cm of the closest lateral skin margin  Sectioning beneath the scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm centrally hemorrhagic biopsy which is outlined by a firm rim of indurated fibrotic parenchyma  The biopsy cavity is located 3 7cm from the closest deep margin  6 0cm from both the closest inferior and superior margins  8 5cm from the closest lateral margin  and 11 5cm from the closest medial margin  The remaining parenchyma is composed predominantly of unremarkable adipose tissue with scant areas of fibrous septae  No additional anomalies are noted  Section code  A C  representative sections of hemorrhagic biopsy