rogesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm breast biopsy  with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm skin ellipse attached  The short stitch designates superior  and a long stitch designates lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm  tan white  gritty  stellate lesion 0 2cm from the superior inked resection margin  The mass is 2 0cm from the deep resection margin  0 6cm from the lateral resection margin  3 0cm from the medial resection margin  and 1 8cm from the inferior resection margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The skin ellipse is unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A C  representative sections of tumor in relation to superior inked resection margin DandE  representative sections of fibrosis with ink on superolateral resection margin F  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on lateral resection margin G  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on medial resection H  representative section of breast parenchyma with ink on medial and inferior margins I  representative sections of skin ellipse  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axilla   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of fibrofatty tissue with fragments of skeletal muscle attached  Numerous soft  freely moveable lymph nodes  measuring from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm in greatest dimensions are identified  Lymph nodes are submitted in J through R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  Thomas J Lynch  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST LUMP PART B  RIGHT AXILLA CONTENTS   report_end  , No.
