ical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with localization wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm rubbery  tan  slightly translucent  well circumscribed nodule  located less than 0 1cm from the inked resection margin  Representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX  1  resubmitted in cassette A  The entire remaining sections are submitted in cassettes B through I  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  CONSISTENT WITH COLLOID CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENT FOR FURTHER SAMPLING TO RULE OUT DUCTAL COMPONENT  O R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , No.
