Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 49 CLINICAL DATA  Density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  WITH SEVERAL FOCI SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1    SOLID TYPE  3  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 10 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a piece of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm with localizing needle in place  An X ray accompanies the specimen  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm red area  Representative sections frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  Breast section adjacent to tissue from which frozen is taken in B  The rest of the specimen in C through G  Resident  KEITH KWAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  EXCISIONAL  BREAST CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST , No.
