 positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a firm white area measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  0 2cm from the closest margin  A representative section from the suspicious area is frozen as FX  1  now A  The remainder of the lesion is in B D  Additional representative sections of the surrounding tissue are in E and F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen containing an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple and a 6 0cm sutured recent incision  The specimen is irregular  such that there is significantly more tissue in the superior lateral region  In addition  posterior to the ellipse  beneath the recent incision is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm apparently exposed biopsy cavity  which is inked green  The margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal soft white parenchyma in the region of the biopsy cavity  The closest margin to the biopsy site is 1cm  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty  with an area of localized fibrous and cystic change  1 0cm inferior and medial to the nipple  Representative sections of the biopsy cavity are submitted from medial to lateral in G K  w