as 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 18     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm white pink breast tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal predominantly white breast parenchyma  No area grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section done  Submitted entirely in A through J with area near tip of wire in B and C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   needle loc    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of firm  yellow pink breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm nodule  a fine stellate white tissue with hemorrhagic streaks and calcifications near localizing wire  The nodule reaches the margin in multiple points  A section is frozen as FX 1  Submitted entirely in K through P  Frozen saved for Cox 5  Tissue submitted for Dr  Sgroi  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS ONLY   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis b