 a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm area and range from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm in greatest dimension  The nodules come to 0 2cm of the posterior margin  The nodules are diffuse and are also located in patches throughout the remaining mammary tissue  One of these patches measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm and is located in the subareolar anterolateral breast tissue  This area focally abuts the anterior margin  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals several possible tan pink lymph nodes averaging 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Subareolar anterolateral breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mid lower  central inferior  breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Scar  lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between scar and nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodular area in lower outer breast tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from axillary tail which may represent lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  axillary contents left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan pink fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal several tan pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 6cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three intact lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled  final lateral margin left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan pink  fibrofatty tissue with a black stitch along one aspect designating the new margin  The stitched aspect is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal focal hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormality  The specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast re excision skin   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink skin ellipse  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  The margin is inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned and representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   E